From 8f83a89b2ab7342d9a0554e1257ed6c3f61f1089 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mark-vis <118430440+mark-vis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 22:19:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 13/14] Add tagging sockets for sub-floats

Request for comments: a tagging interface for sub-floats (sub-figures,
sub-tables with their own caption, as made by subcaption).
latex-lab-float said that these "will be implemented as simple Part with
their own Caption"; this commit proposes how packages can ask for that.

lttagging declares three tagging sockets without arguments (the float
type is \@captype):

- subfloat/box: "the next minipage or \parbox is a sub-float". That box
  gets the structure float/<type>/sub (role Part) instead of its Div,
  and a caption inside it becomes its first kid. It is used directly
  before the box and acts only once: boxes nested in the sub-float and
  later boxes, also in the same group, are normal. No group is needed:
  the settings of the sub-float end with the box.
- subfloat/begin and subfloat/end: open and close the structure of a
  sub-float that is not a single box (in vertical mode, inside the box).

\DeclareTaggingFloatType also declares float/<type>/sub (role Part),
and latex-lab-namespace has float/figure/sub, float/table/sub and
float/generic/sub.

The plugs in latex-lab-float start the structure, set
\@current@float@struct to its number and set the float target
\@floatHref@<type> to empty locally, so that the sub-caption gets a
target of its own instead of the target of the float. The plug of
subfloat/box assigns (locally) the plugs subfloat to minipage/before
and parbox/before, which restore the previous plugs and start the
sub-float structure in place of the Div. Each use of subfloat/box
takes a new number, which the first box uses up, so a later box in the
same group gets the previous plug (a minipage restores the plugs only
inside its own group). It does nothing if the tagging code of
latex-lab-minipage is not active. The first two lines of these plugs
repeat the kernel plugs of latex-lab-minipage (a comment there says
so). The plug of parbox/before runs at the group level of the caller,
so for a \parbox it also saves \@current@float@struct, the float target
and the plug of parbox/after, and assigns (locally) a plug subfloat to
parbox/after that restores them after the box; otherwise a \caption of
the float after an ungrouped \parbox sub-float would become a kid of
the sub-float and make its own target. A minipage needs no such step,
because its plug runs inside the group of the environment.

Open questions for the team: whether sub-floats belong in the kernel
interface at all, the names of the sockets and structures, the role
Part, and whether subfloat/box (which relies on the plugs of the
minipage and parbox sockets) is acceptable or only begin/end should be
offered.

Without tagging nothing changes. New latex-lab test float-020 (\caption
and \caption* in floats with hyperref, sub-floats as minipage
environment with a footnote, nested minipage and \caption*, as \parbox,
with begin/end inside a minipage, and a normal minipage after them;
only the first of several boxes after subfloat/box, with and without a
group, is a sub-float; a \caption after an ungrouped \parbox sub-float
with a normal and a nested \parbox sub-float inside belongs to the
float and uses the float target).
